  "notes": "The noun {経過|けいか} is used even more frequently than the verb form, especially in medical and administrative contexts to describe how something has been progressing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {時間|じかん}が{経過|けいか}する: time passes\n- {経過|けいか}{観察|かんさつ}: follow-up observation (medical)\n- {経過|けいか}{報告|ほうこく}: progress report\n- {経過|けいか}{良好|りょうこう}: favorable progress\n- {経過|けいか}{措置|そち}: transitional measure\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {過|す}ぎる: to pass — everyday word for time passing\n- {経|た}つ: to pass, elapse — common native Japanese word for time passing\n- {進行|しんこう}する: to progress, advance — emphasizes forward movement\n- {推移|すいい}する: to shift, transition — focuses on gradual changes over time",
